From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] zink: no push descriptors on MoltenVK

What: zink turns KHR_push_descriptor off when the (layered) driver is
MoltenVK, like it already does on AMD.

Why: MoltenVK binds push descriptor sets as discrete Metal resources, never
through argument buffers. zink declares its bo bindings as several typed
arrays aliasing one binding (u32 and u64 views of the kernel inputs), and
SPIRV-Cross can alias an array binding only inside an argument buffer. So
every compute shader that reads the push set failed in MoltenVK with
"Attempting to alias same binding with a descriptor array which is not
implemented through argument buffers" (vkCreateComputePipelines ->
VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED): no OpenCL kernel (rusticl) ran at all.
Seen on Venus over MoltenVK 1.4.2 (OmacVM.app, macOS 15); zink directly on
MoltenVK has the same problem.

Upstream: upstreamable (Mesa zink), not sent.
Test: src/app/guest/venus/cltest.c (saxpy + reduction, PASS) and clpeak;
before the patch every kernel failed to build its pipeline.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
@@ -3136,6 +3136,14 @@
    }
 
    switch (zink_driverid(screen)) {
+   case VK_DRIVER_ID_MOLTENVK:
+      /* MoltenVK binds push descriptor sets as discrete Metal resources, never
+       * through argument buffers, and SPIRV-Cross can only alias one binding
+       * with several types (zink's bo arrays) inside an argument buffer: every
+       * shader reading the push set would fail to compile.
+       */
+      screen->info.have_KHR_push_descriptor = false;
+      break;
    case VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_RADV:
    case VK_DRIVER_ID_AMD_OPEN_SOURCE:
    case VK_DRIVER_ID_AMD_PROPRIETARY:
